<!-- PendulumPump-v0: the pendulum reduced model of the two-agent coop suite
     (see callosum/envs/coop/pendulum.py and callosum/configs/coop_tasks.PendulumConfig).

Model layout (PLAN.md "Two-robot task suite"):
  * `bob` -- a 0.5 kg sphere (radius 0.06 m) on ONE hinge about world +y, hanging 0.5 m
             below the fixed pivot at the world origin (the sphere's body-frame offset is
             `pos="0 0 -0.5"`, so its centre of mass is the pendulum bob).

The two agents act through `mujoco.mjData.xfrc_applied` TORQUE on the bob's hinge: the
`left` actuator commands only a positive world-y torque, the `right` actuator only a
negative one (the env's one-sided actuation). The spec allows either one-sided forces on
the bob or one-sided hinge torques; the torque variant is used because it is the cleanest
reduced model of the pumping task (no contact anywhere, no force application point to
model). There are deliberately NO actuators, NO cameras and NO contacts.

XML-OWNED physics: the bob mass, its radius and the 0.5 m length (the body-frame offset of
the sphere). MuJoCo derives the body inertia from the geom at compile time and `mj_setConst`
does not recompute it when `body_mass` is written at runtime, so the mass/length stay
XML-owned; `PendulumConfig` documents them and is the source of truth for everything else
(timestep, gravity, hinge limit, damping, armature, torque authority), which `PendulumEnv`
writes into the model. The damping/armature values below are defaults only; each reset
replaces the hinge damping with the episode's sampled randomisation.
-->
<mujoco model="pendulum_coop">
  <compiler angle="radian"/>
  <option timestep="0.005" integrator="implicitfast" gravity="0 0 -9.81"/>

  <worldbody>
    <body name="bob" pos="0 0 0">
      <joint name="pivot_hinge" type="hinge" axis="0 1 0" range="-3.0 3.0" limited="true"
             damping="0.1" armature="0.001"/>
      <geom name="bob_geom" type="sphere" size="0.06" mass="0.5" pos="0 0 -0.5"
            contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
